From: buntOS contributors
Subject: [PATCH] spmi: mtk-pmif: fix the RCS interrupt bank calculation

Each SPMI_SLV_x_y_EINT register holds the RCS interrupt status of four
slaves, eight bits each, as mtk_spmi_rcs_irq_eoi() already assumes. The
chained handler divides the bit number by 7 instead of 8 to find the
slave, so a status bit at position 7, 14-15, 21-23 or 28-31 is taken for
the next slave. The handler then clears the wrong byte, the bit stays set,
and the loop never ends.

Divide by 8.

Fixes: ab1b3469fc28 ("spmi: mtk-pmif: Implement Request Capable Slave (RCS) interrupt")
---
diff --git a/drivers/spmi/spmi-mtk-pmif.c b/drivers/spmi/spmi-mtk-pmif.c
index 833c2b3..ef3cf4e 100644
--- a/drivers/spmi/spmi-mtk-pmif.c
+++ b/drivers/spmi/spmi-mtk-pmif.c
@@ -513,7 +513,7 @@ static void mtk_spmi_handle_chained_irq(struct irq_desc *desc)
 
 		while (val) {
 			u8 bit = __ffs(val);
-			u8 bank = bit / 7;
+			u8 bank = bit / 8;
 			u8 sid = ((i - SPMI_SLV_3_0_EINT) * 4) + bank;
 
 			val &= ~(PMIF_RCS_IRQ_MASK << (8 * bank));
